From: ps3 <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:03:33 +0300
Subject: porting: malloc_trim threshold from LU_TRIM_MB (default 256 MiB,
 unchanged)

Luanti trims glibc's arenas from its emerge and mesh threads once 256 MiB of map blocks, voxel
manipulators and meshes were freed. On a PS3 (~217 MB of RAM) that never happens: a 2026-10-18
profile showed 23-28 MB free inside the arenas, 18-22 MB of it in one thread arena, resident
or swapped out. LU_TRIM_MB=N trims every N MiB freed instead.

diff --git a/src/porting.cpp b/src/porting.cpp
--- a/src/porting.cpp
+++ b/src/porting.cpp
@@ -964,7 +964,15 @@ double perf_freq = get_perf_freq();
 
 static std::atomic<size_t> memory_freed;
 
-constexpr size_t MEMORY_TRIM_THRESHOLD = 256 * 1024 * 1024;
+// LU_TRIM_MB (environment): the threshold in MiB, 256 when unset. A PS3 has ~217 MB of RAM in
+// all: 256 MB freed between trims never comes, and the holes swap out instead (docs/MEMORY.md).
+static size_t memoryTrimThreshold()
+{
+	const char *s = getenv("LU_TRIM_MB");
+	long mb = s && *s ? strtol(s, nullptr, 10) : 0;
+	return (size_t)(mb > 0 ? mb : 256) * 1024 * 1024;
+}
+static const size_t MEMORY_TRIM_THRESHOLD = memoryTrimThreshold();
 
 void TrackFreedMemory(size_t amount)
 {
